# clemacs allowed skips for ELisp loads
#
# One relative path per line; comments allowed. Keep reasons and dates.
# Use this for files that are intentionally out of scope (GUI/nativecomp/modules)
# or temporarily blocked; prefer shrinking this list over time.

# 2026-01-05: Defer legacy non-Unicode encodings; focus on UTF-8/editor bring-up.
lisp/international/cp51932.el
lisp/international/eucjp-ms.el

# 2026-01-10: UTF-8-only is a hard constraint for clemacs; legacy encodings and
# input-method catalogs (LEIM) must not gate bring-up/milestones.

# 2026-01-08: Start bringing up nadvice under startup manifests (see
# startup.*.files max-forms checkpoints); keep this list for intentionally
# out-of-scope files only.

# 2026-01-08: Defer LEIM/input-method registration; for now we only care about
# UTF-8 working end-to-end (load/edit/save). Revisit once editor core is solid.
lisp/leim/leim-list.el

# 2026-01-11: GUI-only / non-TTY pdump conditionals (TTY-only build; no GUI backends).
# - dnd/tool-bar/dynamic-setting are only loaded when `x-create-frame` exists
#   and/or GUI features are present in admin/pdump-common.el.
lisp/dnd.el
lisp/tool-bar.el
lisp/dynamic-setting.el

# 2026-01-11: Non-supported platform (MS-DOS/PC console window-system).
lisp/term/pc-win.el

# 2026-01-11: Loaded only when `x-create-frame` exists (GUI builds); out of scope
# for TTY-only clemacs bring-up.
lisp/mwheel.el

# NOTE: Keep this list strictly "out-of-scope only". If a file is in-scope but
# currently failing to load, prefer using `startup.*.files` max-forms caps and
# implement missing primitives instead of skipping.
